From a0d3351bb5f460b956d23e5e3897bc78660d4718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:42:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable periodic SSE keep-alive heartbeats and shield
 streaming abort cleanup

Long queued or cold-prefill streaming requests (200K-1M context) can wait
15-175s before the first token arrives, causing reverse proxies and HTTP
clients to drop idle SSE connections. Meanwhile, Starlette's StreamingResponse
runs inside its own AnyIO task group after @with_cancellation returns the
response object, so client disconnects during streaming prefill or send()
repeatedly cancel the body task on every event-loop tick and interrupt
AsyncLLM.abort() before engine_core.abort_requests_async() completes.

1. Enable SSE keep-alive comment heartbeats (': keep-alive\n\n') by default at
   15.0s across /v1/chat/completions, /v1/completions, /v1/responses, and
   /v1/messages, configurable via VLLM_SSE_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL_S (or <=0 to
   disable) and --sse-keep-alive-interval.
2. Replace per-token asyncio.wait({next_task}, timeout=interval) in
   _keep_alive_stream with an eager-start task and a single rolling
   loop.call_at timer, cutting per-chunk wrapper overhead by 69-88% under
   uvloop without cancelling in-flight anext(generator) awaits.
3. Shield streaming generator finalization, load_aware_call body_iterator
   closure, and AsyncLLM.abort() engine_core.abort_requests_async() with
   anyio.CancelScope(shield=True) + cancellation-resilient wait loops so
   client disconnects during prefill or send() deterministically abort the
   in-flight engine request before decrementing server_load_metrics.

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354, following Candidate
1107 patch_head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488.
Quality: no model arithmetic, scheduler, context, sampling, or SSE data-frame
change; SSE comment lines starting with ':' are ignored by WhatWG SSE and
OpenAI/Anthropic SDK parsers.
Tests: 71/71 tests pass across 2 container boots in test_api_cancellation.py,
test_request_submission_cleanup.py, and test_utility_call_cleanup.py; 2-boot
uvloop benchmarks confirm 3.04-3.22x higher ASGI streaming throughput vs the
prior asyncio.wait loop and 32/32 completed engine aborts on disconnect.
Upstream status: local candidate patch 0762 on top of 1107.
